WEBVTT

00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:10,040
Hello everybody. This is Dr. Kevin Cutters and in this video in this section of our website, we're going to talk about gastrointestinal cancers.

00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:24,040
Now your GI system really starts in the mouth and ends where you deposit feces in the toilet, but in this section, we're really going to talk about the cancers from your stomach down.

00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:33,040
Now your GI cancers are named after the area that the cancer has found and the cell type that the cancer has found.

00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:37,040
It's important to understand when we're talking about any cancer.

00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:46,040
If I have rectal cancer and it metastasizes to my liver, it's not liver cancer. Now it's still rectal cancer that's metastasized to my liver.

00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:55,040
So it's still those cells that cell type of the original spot, that origin of the cancer that is metastasized.

00:00:55,040 --> 00:01:06,040
So liver cancer is cancer of the liver cells. Rectal cancer or another cancer is cancer of those other cells that may metastasize to a different area.

00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:14,040
So we can have metastasized cancer to the GI tract. Then it's not primary. It's secondary. It's metastasized cancer.

00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:20,040
So in this section, we're talking about primary GI cancers of the stomach on down.

00:01:20,040 --> 00:01:32,040
So those are named after the cell type that is found in the biopsy and named after the area of where the primary cancer was found.

00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:38,040
Whether it's small intestine, gastric cancer, anal cancer, appendiceal cancer and so on.

00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:53,040
Now it can be very difficult when you get a diagnosis of any type of cancer on deciding what to do. Many people are hurting down a pathway that quite frankly they may regret down the road.

00:01:53,040 --> 00:02:01,040
My recommendation for everybody, when you get a diagnosis of cancer, it's very scary. I know I've been there.

00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:15,040
But when you get a diagnosis of cancer, the best thing to do is to slow down. Don't make any rash judgments and grave decisions that you may want to.

00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:21,040
There's nothing you can do to change if you go into surgery. It's done. You can't undo that.

00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:31,040
So you can always do surgery. You can always do chemo. You can always do radiation. But you always have more time than usually than what you're told.

00:02:31,040 --> 00:02:38,040
Not that you're supposed to stick your head on the sand and pretend it's not there, but slow down. Take a little time. Do some research.

00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:51,040
It's also important to understand that when you're considering chemo radiation, surgery or whatever else that you can't also do alternative care at the same time.

00:02:51,040 --> 00:03:03,040
And quite frankly, that's probably going to be your best bet to help improve the outcome. I'm not against doing chemo radiation, surgery or immunotherapy or something combination thereof.

00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:28,040
If it's the right thing for you, but I think it's probably kind of silly not to make some dietary changes and look at nutrition and look at other therapeutic interventions, aka alternative care, that would be wise to help you, even if you do choose to do chemo or radiation or something, it'll help you get through that much better.

00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:37,040
So that's all I'm asking you to do it. And really, that's what our whole website is all about. And that's why we give away my books on this site too.

00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:51,040
So navigate to the free books. Download them. They're free. Not everybody's ever going to be able to come to us, but we feel like we want this clinic to be as much of a ministry as possible so that you can gain knowledge.

00:03:51,040 --> 00:04:07,040
We are called by God to not be foolish and not be ignorant. And of course, that's talking about scriptural things, but it's also talking about how we live our lives or the decisions that we're making that that change in all through our life.

00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:18,040
So adding alternative care to standards of care or doing alternative care prior to doing standards of care. So maybe that you won't need to do that.

00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:27,040
Standard of care that they're recommending at least look into it. That's what this is all about. And when you do look into it, I know it is confusing.

00:04:27,040 --> 00:04:40,040
Should I take, you know, this supplement or that supplement or eat this food or use this type of therapy? Well, please use this in this website as best you can to gain as much knowledge as you can.

00:04:40,040 --> 00:04:46,040
And if you do feel led to schedule a case review with me so that we can talk about it.

00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:59,040
Ultimately, we want you to have the best results possible, the best outcome possible from this diagnosis. And that's really what our goal is for you.

00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:07,040
So utilize this site, utilize our free material and please be blessed by it. We're always here for you.

